Subject: Cantor Held-Out Attention Language Calibration Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 2d284e26-df13-45a8-9e8e-ecf44175899b
@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Held_Out_Attention_Language_Calibration.sop

& [Problem] is an observed generalization gap
  + exact structured identity and transition forms repeatedly cross the unchanged gate
  + ordinary paraphrases remain sensitive to wording
  + the current pinned suite proves fixed fixtures and does not map the wider ingress surface

& [Decision] is a frozen-checkpoint observation harness
  + measure previously unseen prompts after committing the runtime
  + preserve procedure choice and argument extraction as separate outcomes
  + keep corpus, harness, and aggregate evidence outside the trusted deployment
  + retain exact case evidence and descriptive metrics without adapting during observation

& [RejectedAlternatives] remain outside authority
  + lowering the confidence threshold weakens the security boundary instead of measuring routing
  + editing procedure descriptions before measuring destroys the frozen baseline
  + treating the same-author corpus as an independent benchmark overstates evidence
  + invoking the full Cantor and llama.cpp path adds cost and semantic variability unrelated to selector calibration

& [ExpectedValue] is an empirical attention-language map
  + identify which natural, imperative, explicit, key-value, and JSON-like forms preserve procedure identity
  + distinguish selection failures from argument extraction failures
  + provide evidence for later procedure-description or grammar revisions under a new governed checkpoint
